-- Migration 24 (down): remove GraphRAG-03B durable deletion state.
--
-- Removes ONLY the GraphRAG-specific event and tombstone table. The canonical
-- `source` table, the existing `source_delete` vector-cleanup event, and all
-- unrelated schema are left untouched. After this runs, the source delete path
-- returns byte-for-byte to baseline.
--
-- Removing the table drops any still-pending tombstone rows -- removing the
-- GraphRAG feature removes its local lifecycle metadata cleanly. This does NOT
-- purge any copy already held by a remote LightRAG sidecar; remote purge is a
-- GraphRAG-03C/03D operational concern, not a schema rollback.

REMOVE EVENT IF EXISTS graphrag_source_delete ON TABLE source;
REMOVE TABLE IF EXISTS graphrag_deletion;
